{ Original Hippopotamus as Black course. Study material, not a historical game. Choose the course move, explain its purpose and name one opposing resource. Other playable moves may exist; this is a repertoire-recall question. ANSWER: Course move: 10... Ne7. This illustrative route shows the recognizable formation when White develops quietly. The knights avoid blocking the fianchetto bishops, but Black has used many pawn tempi and is still uncastled. White owns more space and can prepare d5, e5 or a wing attack. Finishing the diagram is not a strategic achievement if Black then has no active move. } 10... Ne7 *

