{ Original Hippopotamus as Black course. Study material, not a historical game. Choose the course move, explain its purpose and name one opposing resource. Other playable moves may exist; this is a repertoire-recall question. ANSWER: Course move: 7... e6. The bishop on e2 is less directly aimed at h7 than on d3, but White can support a central advance without exposing pieces. Black preserves flexibility. White may use Bf1, a4 and d5 to squeeze. A lack of immediate threats is not permission for unlimited waiting. } 7... e6 8. Be3 Nf6 9. e5 dxe5 10. Nxe5 *

