{ Original Hippopotamus as Black course. Study material, not a historical game. Name the side to move, describe the central structure and give a plan for your course side. Name the opponent's most relevant counterplay. No single move is required. ANSWER: White to move. White king g1; central-file pawns c2, f2, d4, e4. Black king e8; central-file pawns d6, e6, c7, f7. Compare the pawn contacts and opened files before choosing a move. Branch plan to reassess: Decide on king safety and a central break. Examine ...c5 against d4 and ...d5 against e4; neither move is compulsory or safe in every version. White owns more space and can prepare d5, e5 or a wing attack. Finishing the diagram is not a strategic achievement if Black then has no active move. Check which threats remain possible in this exact diagram. } *

